# Copy to `.env.local` to change how the app talks to its API.
#
# The default (`msw`) needs no setup and no backend: a service worker answers
# requests from IndexedDB, which is the mode the deployed demo runs in and the
# one the ENTNT assignment brief calls for.

# msw  — mock service worker + Dexie/IndexedDB, no server required
# http — the ASP.NET Core backend in server/ (see server/README.md to run it)
VITE_API_MODE=msw

# Where http mode sends requests. Left as the relative default, Vite proxies
# /api to VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET in development, which avoids CORS entirely and
# keeps the bundle free of an absolute URL.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
# VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:5180
